18. Revision History

* Version 1.0.0, effective 2026-06-03, was the initial independent
  viewing-only license for the Original Materials.

* Version 1.0.1, effective 2026-06-04, clarified that third-party
  legal material is organized under third-party/ and that local
  application-managed runtime data and application output remain
  outside Original Materials except where they include protected
  repository content.

* Version 1.0.2, effective 2026-06-10, strengthened viewing
  limitations, ordinary application use limitations, prohibited
  conduct, artificial-intelligence and dataset restrictions, bundled
  resource and distribution treatment, provenance-sensitive material
  treatment, controlling-text rules, termination consequences,
  severability, and non-waiver provisions.

* Version 1.0.3, effective 2026-06-10, added Japanese governing law,
  Tokyo District Court exclusive first-instance forum language, and
  hosting-service terms clarification.

* Version 1.0.4, effective 2026-06-11, recast the License in a more
  formal rights-reservation structure and clarified the distinction
  between viewing, ordinary application use, User Materials,
  Application Output, Original Materials, Third-Party Materials,
  Distribution Materials, and hosting-service functionality.

* Version 1.0.5, effective 2026-06-13, recorded consolidated
  third-party attribution handling and separated third-party license
  texts from the license governing the Original Materials.

* Version 2.0.0, effective 2026-06-13, reorganized the License around
  formal definitions of License, Licensor, Licensee, Legal Entity,
  Source Form, Object Form, Work, Derivative Work, Original Materials,
  Repository Contents, Third-Party Materials, Provenance-Sensitive
  Materials, User Materials, Application Output, Contribution,
  Distribution Materials, Ordinary Application Use, and AI Use.

* Version 2.1.0, effective 2026-06-13, consolidated the grant into one
  limited-grant section, reduced repeated prohibitory wording by
  relying on defined terms, removed references to an unnecessary
  auxiliary root document, and kept README as the only explanatory
  repository document that shares the definitions stated in this
  License.

* Version 2.2.0, effective 2026-06-14, expanded the definitions to add
  Maintainer, Current Repository, License Text, Third-Party License
  Text, Desktop Distribution, Official Distribution, External
  Contribution, Contribution Materials, Public Issue, Private
  Reporting Channel, Security Report, Security Reporting Policy,
  Security Testing, and GitHub Platform Terms; renamed User Materials
  to User-Created Materials; replaced the short name Application with
  Ludoxel; and aligned the contribution, security reporting,
  distribution, controlling-text, and platform-terms provisions with
  those definitions.

* Version 2.3.0, effective 2026-06-15, tightened the legal character,
  limited grant, repository-visibility, distribution, and GitHub
  platform-terms language into a more declarative rights-boundary
  form; corrected non-ASCII spacing in the Licensee definition; and
  preserved the existing all-rights-reserved scope.

* Version 2.4.0, effective 2026-06-19, added the Documentation Site to
  the definitions, limited grant, rights reservations, excluded uses,
  distribution treatment, hosting treatment, disclaimers, liability
  limits, governing-law provisions, and controlling-text provisions;
  clarified that public website availability, static-site output,
  previews, and hosting-service features do not grant reuse,
  redistribution, scraping, mirroring, deployment, or AI Use rights;
  and preserved the all-rights-reserved control of the Original
  Materials.
